[38;2;124;124;124mThe assertion: If $x$ is a cluster point of a filter $\mathcal{F}$, then $x$ is [0m[38;2;124;124;124ma limit of a filter $\mathcal{F'}$ that is finer than $\mathcal{F}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me recall the definitions from Engelking:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m- A **filter** on a set $X$ is a non-empty family of subsets of $X$ that does [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mnot contain the empty set, is closed under finite intersections, and is upward [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mclosed (if $F \in \mathcal{F}$ and $F \subseteq G$, then $G \in \mathcal{F}$).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m- A **cluster point** of a filter $\mathcal{F}$: $x$ is a cluster point of $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathcal{F}$ if $x \in \overline{F}$ for every $F \in \mathcal{F}$. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mEquivalently, every neighborhood of $x$ intersects every member of $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathcal{F}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m- A **limit point** of a filter $\mathcal{F}$: $x$ is a limit of $\mathcal{F}$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mif every neighborhood of $x$ belongs to $\mathcal{F}$. Equivalently, the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mneighborhood filter $\mathcal{N}(x) \subseteq \mathcal{F}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m- A filter $\mathcal{F'}$ is **finer than** $\mathcal{F}$ if $\mathcal{F} [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\subseteq \mathcal{F'}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow the claim: If $x$ is a cluster point of $\mathcal{F}$, then there exists a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfilter $\mathcal{F'} \supseteq \mathcal{F}$ such that $x$ is a limit of $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathcal{F'}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor $x$ to be a limit of $\mathcal{F'}$, we need $\mathcal{N}(x) \subseteq [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathcal{F'}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo we need $\mathcal{F'} \supseteq \mathcal{F} \cup \mathcal{N}(x)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor such a filter to exist, we need $\mathcal{F} \cup \mathcal{N}(x)$ to have [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe finite intersection property (FIP), i.e., no finite subcollection has empty [0m[38;2;124;124;124mintersection.[0m

